**Definition 10.1 (three different transition contracts).** Fix $P$ and
put $\mathcal C_P=\bigcup_{N\ge1}\mathcal C_{P,N}$, with edge domain
$\mathcal C^-_P=\bigcup_{N\ge1}\mathcal C^-_{P,N}$. A supplemental
encoding is any function $z:\mathcal C_P\to Z$, even one chosen with
full mathematical knowledge of a concrete cut. Its augmented state is
$\eta(s)=(O^+(s),z(s))$. An exact deterministic realization supplies
one update $T$ on the realized edge domain satisfying

$$
T(\eta(s))=\eta(Fs),\qquad s\in\mathcal C^-_P.
$$

The update receives only that augmented state and represents one native
row. In particular it receives no omitted annex contents or external
history. Arbitrary computation within this mathematical update is
allowed. Actual row labels may additionally be retained; the obstruction
already holds for the weaker demand displaying just $O^+$ successors.

For a nondeterministic realization, require **exact projected response
sets**: from $\eta(s_{N,m,k})$, for every horizon
$0\le h\le D_{P,N}-k$, the set of projected successor sequences of
length $h$ is exactly the singleton

$$
\left\{\bigl(O^+(s_{N,m,k+1}),\ldots,
                  O^+(s_{N,m,k+h})\bigr)\right\}.
$$

This includes existence, excludes spurious sequences and retains every
intermediate successor. Requiring only that each actual projected
sequence is included is **permissive forward inclusion**, a weaker
contract. These definitions concern native projected dynamics, not
the original $Q$ or its action-admission relation.

